<title>UK: FORECAST - Results of UK interest rate and tax poll.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Results of UK interest rate and tax poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the tabulated results of a Reuters survey on expectations for UK base rate at end-1996 and end-June 1997, and the size of likely tax cuts in this year's November Budget.</p>
<p>The survey was carried out after confirmation on Thursday that rates were left on hold at 5.75 percent after this month's monetary meeting. A total of 20 economists contributed.</p>
<p>Fourteen economists said base rates would not be cut again in this cycle while six forecast a 25 basis point cut to 5.50 percent. One of the 14 forecast a 50 b.p. rise by December.</p>
<p>Also included are their forecasts of the net tax giveaway in the budget due to be announced by Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke on November 26.</p>
